(
  'Company Registration in India: Types, Process, Costs, and Timeline',
  'Complete guide to company registration in India. Compare Private Limited, LLP, OPC, and Partnership structures. Know the exact process, required documents, and registration costs.',
  'Choosing the right business structure is one of the most important decisions for any entrepreneur. It affects your liability, taxes, compliance requirements, and ability to raise funding. Here is a comprehensive guide to company registration in India.\n\n## Types of Business Structures in India\n\n### 1. Private Limited Company\n- **Minimum members:** 2 directors, 2 shareholders\n- **Liability:** Limited to shareholding\n- **Ideal for:** Startups seeking funding, scalable businesses\n- **Compliance:** Higher (annual ROC filings, audits)\n- **Tax rate:** 22% (existing) or 15% (new manufacturing)\n\n### 2. Limited Liability Partnership (LLP)\n- **Minimum members:** 2 designated partners\n- **Liability:** Limited (partners not personally liable)\n- **Ideal for:** Professional services (CA, lawyers, consultants)\n- **Compliance:** Lower than Pvt Ltd\n- **Tax rate:** 30% + surcharge\n\n### 3. One Person Company (OPC)\n- **Members:** 1 director, 1 nominee\n- **Liability:** Limited\n- **Ideal for:** Solo entrepreneurs wanting corporate status\n- **Restriction:** Turnover cannot exceed ₹2 crore\n\n### 4. Partnership Firm\n- **Members:** 2-20 partners\n- **Liability:** Unlimited (partners personally liable)\n- **Ideal for:** Small businesses with trusted partners\n- **Compliance:** Minimal\n\n## Private Limited Company Registration: Step-by-Step\n\n**Step 1: Obtain DSC**\nAll proposed directors must obtain Digital Signature Certificate.\n\n**Step 2: Apply for DIN**\nDirector Identification Number is obtained from MCA portal.\n\n**Step 3: Name Approval**\nApply for name reservation through RUN (Reserve Unique Name) on MCA portal.\n\n**Step 4: File SPICe+ Form**\nThe integrated form incorporates the company, applies for PAN, TAN, GST, EPF, and ESIC simultaneously.\n\n**Step 5: Draft MOA and AOA**\nMemorandum and Articles of Association define the company scope and internal rules.\n\n**Step 6: Certificate of Incorporation**\nMCA issues the Certificate of Incorporation (COI) with CIN. Your company is officially registered.\n\n## Documents Required\n\n**For Directors:**\n- PAN card\n- Aadhaar card\n- Recent bank statement / utility bill (for address proof)\n- Passport size photo\n- Email ID and mobile number\n\n**For Registered Office:**\n- Utility bill (not older than 2 months)\n- NOC from property owner\n- Rental agreement (if applicable)\n\n## Timeline and Costs\n\n| Activity | Time |\n|----------|------|\n| DSC | 1-2 days |\n| Name approval | 1-3 days |\n| SPICe+ filing | 1 day |\n| Certificate of Incorporation | 5-7 working days |\n| **Total** | **7-14 days** |\n\nGovernment fees depend on authorized share capital. Professional charges for end-to-end incorporation (including MCA fees, professional charges, and stamp duty) typically range from ₹7,000 to ₹15,000.\n\n## Post-Incorporation Compliance\n\n- Open current bank account\n- Obtain GST registration (if applicable)\n- File DIR-3 KYC annually\n- File annual returns with ROC (AOC-4, MGT-7)\n- Conduct annual general meetings\n- Maintain statutory registers',
  'Business', 'Neha Gupta', '🏢', '10 min read',
  'Company Registration in India 2025: Pvt Ltd, LLP, OPC Process & Cost | GST Tax Wale',
  'Complete guide to company registration in India. Compare Pvt Ltd, LLP, OPC. Know exact process, required documents, timeline and costs.',
  'company registration India, private limited company, LLP registration, OPC, business registration, MCA',
  1, NOW()
),
(
  'GST ITC Reconciliation: How to Match GSTR-2B and Avoid Notice',
  'Learn the correct method to reconcile Input Tax Credit between your purchase register and GSTR-2B to avoid GST notices and interest demands.',
  'One of the biggest challenges for GST taxpayers is Input Tax Credit (ITC) reconciliation. If ITC claimed in GSTR-3B does not match GSTR-2B, it can trigger automated notices and interest demands.\n\n## What is GSTR-2B?\n\nGSTR-2B is a static auto-populated statement showing ITC available to you based on returns filed by your suppliers. It is generated on the 14th of every month.\n\n**Key difference from GSTR-2A:** GSTR-2B is static (does not change once generated), while GSTR-2A updates dynamically.\n\n## Why ITC Reconciliation Matters\n\nSection 16(2)(aa) of CGST Act now mandates that ITC can only be claimed if:\n1. The invoice appears in GSTR-2B\n2. Tax has been paid by the supplier\n3. Goods/services have been received\n\nClaiming ITC not reflected in GSTR-2B leads to:\n- Automatic reversal demands\n- Interest @24% per annum\n- Potential cancellation of registration\n\n## 5-Step ITC Reconciliation Process\n\n**Step 1: Download GSTR-2B**\nDownload your GSTR-2B from the GST portal for the month in Excel/JSON format.\n\n**Step 2: Prepare Purchase Register**\nExtract all purchase invoices for the month with GSTIN, invoice number, date, and IGST/CGST/SGST amounts.\n\n**Step 3: Match Invoices**\nCompare each invoice in your purchase register with GSTR-2B entries. Identify:\n- **Matched invoices:** Claim ITC immediately\n- **In books but not in GSTR-2B:** Do not claim; follow up with supplier\n- **In GSTR-2B but not in books:** Verify receipt and add to records\n\n**Step 4: Resolve Mismatches**\n- Contact supplier to file/correct their GSTR-1\n- If supplier has cancelled or amended invoice, check GSTR-2B for the amendment\n- For supplier who has not filed returns: Track and claim in subsequent months\n\n**Step 5: File GSTR-3B**\nClaim only matched ITC in your GSTR-3B. Document the reconciliation for audit trail.\n\n## ITC That Cannot Be Claimed (Section 17(5))\n\nEven if invoices are in GSTR-2B, ITC is blocked for:\n- Motor vehicles (except for business use in transport, training)\n- Food, beverages, outdoor catering\n- Club memberships, health and fitness services\n- Construction services for immovable property\n- Travel benefits for employees\n\n## Tools for Reconciliation\n\n**Manual reconciliation:** VLOOKUP in Excel (suitable for small businesses)\n**GST reconciliation software:** GSTP tools, Tally, Zoho Books, ClearTax\n**Recommended:** Monthly reconciliation rather than quarterly\n\n## Notice Handling: If You Receive ASMT-10\n\nASMT-10 is the notice for ITC mismatches. Respond within 30 days with:\n- Reconciliation statement\n- Explanation for differences\n- Copy of supplier communications\n- Decision to reverse ITC or reasons for retention',
  'GST', 'CA Mahendra Kumar', '📊', '8 min read',
  'GST ITC Reconciliation Guide: GSTR-2B Matching to Avoid Notices | GST Tax Wale',
  'Learn how to reconcile Input Tax Credit (ITC) with GSTR-2B correctly. Step-by-step guide to avoid GST notices, interest demands and penalties.',
  'ITC reconciliation, GSTR-2B, input tax credit, GST notice, ASMT-10, GST compliance',
