(
  'PAN Card for Business: Why Your Company Needs a Separate PAN',
  'Understand why businesses need a separate PAN, how to apply for company PAN, and what transactions require PAN quoting.',
  'Permanent Account Number (PAN) is not just for individuals — every business entity including companies, LLPs, partnerships, and trusts must have a separate PAN. Here is a comprehensive guide.\n\n## Why Does Your Business Need a Separate PAN?\n\n1. **Tax filing:** Income tax returns for businesses are filed using the entity PAN\n2. **TDS deduction:** Businesses deducting TDS must quote PAN on all TDS certificates\n3. **High-value transactions:** All transactions above ₹50,000 require PAN quoting\n4. **Bank account:** Required for opening business bank accounts\n5. **GST registration:** PAN is mandatory for GST registration\n6. **Import/Export:** Required for IEC (Import Export Code) registration\n\n## Who Must Obtain PAN?\n\n- Private Limited Companies\n- LLPs and Partnership Firms\n- Trusts and NGOs\n- Sole Proprietorships (use owner PAN, but separate is recommended)\n- Foreign companies operating in India\n- HUFs (Hindu Undivided Families)\n\n## How to Apply for Business PAN\n\n**Form 49A:** For Indian entities\n**Form 49AA:** For foreign entities\n\n**Documents Required:**\n- Certificate of Incorporation (for companies/LLPs)\n- Partnership deed (for firms)\n- Trust deed (for trusts)\n- Address proof of registered office\n\n**Where to Apply:**\n- Online: NSDL portal (www.onlineservices.nsdl.com)\n- Offline: TIN Facilitation Centers\n\n**Timeline:** 15-20 working days for physical card; e-PAN in 48 hours.\n\n**Fee:** ₹110 (including GST) for Indian address; ₹1,020 for foreign address.\n\n## When is PAN Quoting Mandatory?\n\n- Opening bank accounts\n- Fixed deposits above ₹50,000\n- Purchase of immovable property above ₹10 lakh\n- Sale of motor vehicles above ₹10 lakh\n- Filing income tax returns\n- TDS certificates\n- Foreign exchange transactions above ₹50,000\n\n## Consequences of Not Having PAN\n\n- TDS deducted at higher rate (20%)\n- Cannot file income tax returns\n- Cannot register for GST\n- Cannot open business bank account\n- Subject to tax penalties\n\n## Updating PAN Details\n\nIf your business name, address, or authorized signatory changes, update your PAN by submitting Form CSF (Change/Correction in PAN Data) to NSDL.',
  'General', 'Vikas Singh', '🪪', '5 min read',
  'PAN Card for Business: Why Your Company Needs PAN & How to Apply | GST Tax Wale',
  'Why businesses need a separate PAN card. How to apply for company, LLP, or partnership PAN. Mandatory PAN transactions and consequences.',
